 "capsule": "The Lan Na Kingdom, founded by King Mangrai with Chiang Mai as capital from 1296, unified the Tai Yuan principalities of the upper Ping and Kok valleys through the 14th–15th centuries, peaking under Tilokarat (r. 1441/42–1487), before Burmese conquest under Bayinnaung ended its independence in 1558, near this window's close.",
